#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we demonstrate how to leverage advanced error-mitigation tools in Qiskit to improve expectation value estimation in noisy quantum experiments.\n"
msgstr "Dalam tutorial ini, kita akan mendemonstrasikan cara memanfaatkan tools error-mitigation tingkat lanjut di Qiskit untuk meningkatkan estimasi expectation value dalam eksperimen kuantum yang noisy.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is propagated noise absorption (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"
msgstr "Apa itu propagated noise absorption (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Propagated noise absorption is a technique for mitigating gate errors by propagating the observable through the inverse noise channel affecting two-qubit gates, resulting in a noise-mitigating observable.*\n"
msgstr "*Propagated noise absorption adalah teknik untuk memitigasi error gate dengan mempropagasikan observable melalui inverse noise channel yang memengaruhi gate dua-qubit, menghasilkan observable yang memitigasi noise.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use quantum error mitigation to extract useful expectation values from noisy quantum hardware without requiring full fault tolerance. PNA specifically focuses on absorbing noise effects into the observable itself rather than modifying the circuit operations.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa menggunakan quantum error mitigation untuk mengekstraksi expectation value yang berguna dari hardware kuantum yang noisy tanpa memerlukan full fault tolerance. PNA secara spesifik berfokus pada menyerap efek noise ke dalam observable itu sendiri alih-alih memodifikasi operasi circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each noisy gate in a quantum circuit can be modeled as an ideal gate followed by a noise channel. PNA learns or characterizes these noise channels and defines their inverses. Instead of inserting the inverse operations into the hardware execution (which is typically infeasible), PNA propagates the inverse noise channels forward through the circuit and applies them to the observable. This process transforms the observable $O$ into a new operator $\\tilde{O}$, such that measuring $\\tilde{O}$ on the noisy circuit yields the same expectation value as measuring $O$ on an ideal, noise-free circuit.\n"
msgstr "Setiap gate yang noisy dalam circuit kuantum bisa dimodelkan sebagai gate ideal yang diikuti oleh noise channel. PNA mempelajari atau mengkarakterisasi noise channel ini dan mendefinisikan inversnya. Alih-alih menyisipkan operasi invers ke dalam eksekusi hardware (yang biasanya tidak feasible), PNA mempropagasikan inverse noise channel maju melalui circuit dan menerapkannya pada observable. Proses ini mengubah observable $O$ menjadi operator baru $\\tilde{O}$, sedemikian rupa sehingga mengukur $\\tilde{O}$ pada circuit yang noisy menghasilkan expectation value yang sama seperti mengukur $O$ pada circuit ideal yang bebas noise.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be summarized as:\n"
"1. Model each noisy gate $u_i$ as an ideal operation followed by a noise channel $\\Lambda_i$.\n"
"2. Learn or estimate each $\\Lambda_i$ using noise characterization tools.\n"
"3. Define and propagate the inverse noise maps $\\Lambda_i^{-1}$ forward through the circuit using Pauli transfer techniques.\n"
"4. Absorb these inverses into the observable, resulting in a noise-mitigated operator $\\tilde{O}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini bisa diringkas sebagai berikut:\n"
"1. Memodelkan setiap gate noisy $u_i$ sebagai operasi ideal yang diikuti oleh noise channel $\\Lambda_i$.\n"
"2. Mempelajari atau memperkirakan setiap $\\Lambda_i$ menggunakan tools karakterisasi noise.\n"
"3. Mendefinisikan dan mempropagasikan inverse noise map $\\Lambda_i^{-1}$ maju melalui circuit menggunakan teknik Pauli transfer.\n"
"4. Menyerap invers ini ke dalam observable, menghasilkan operator yang dimitigasi-noise $\\tilde{O}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the noise is described as a Pauli channel (or more generally as a sparse Pauli-Lindblad channel), this propagation can be performed efficiently using Pauli propagation. Pauli propagation provides a framework for approximating how inverse noise channels transform as they pass through layers of Clifford and non-Clifford operations, while controlling the computational complexity.\n"
msgstr "Ketika noise dideskripsikan sebagai Pauli channel (atau lebih umum sebagai sparse Pauli-Lindblad channel), propagasi ini bisa dilakukan secara efisien menggunakan Pauli propagation. Pauli propagation menyediakan framework untuk mengaproksimasi bagaimana inverse noise channel bertransformasi ketika melewati layer operasi Clifford dan non-Clifford, sambil mengontrol kompleksitas komputasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By shifting the mitigation into the observable, PNA avoids the large sampling overhead that would otherwise come from inserting physical correction operations into the circuit. Instead, the original noisy circuit is executed, while the observable is transformed into a new operator $\\tilde{O}$ whose expectation value cancels the effects of noise.\n"
msgstr "Dengan memindahkan mitigation ke dalam observable, PNA menghindari sampling overhead besar yang seharusnya muncul dari menyisipkan operasi koreksi fisik ke dalam circuit. Sebagai gantinya, circuit noisy yang asli dieksekusi, sementara observable diubah menjadi operator baru $\\tilde{O}$ yang expectation value-nya membatalkan efek noise.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The PNA workflow {#the-pna-workflow}"
msgstr "Alur kerja PNA {#the-pna-workflow}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The process can be understood through the following conceptual stages. The first schematic illustrates a standard noisy experiment.\n"
msgstr "Proses ini bisa dipahami melalui tahapan konseptual berikut. Skema pertama mengilustrasikan eksperimen noisy standar.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Noisy experiment](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/noisy_expt.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Noisy experiment](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/noisy_expt.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we learn the noise model, we can apply its inverse and cancel the noise.\n"
msgstr "Jika kita mempelajari noise model, kita bisa menerapkan inversnya dan membatalkan noise.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Noise-mitigated experiment](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/noise_mitigated_expt.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Noise-mitigated experiment](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/noise_mitigated_expt.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of implementing the inverse noise channel by sampling it on the QPU as in probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), we apply it classically to the measured observable using Pauli propagation. The resulting observable effectively mitigates the learned gate noise when measured.\n"
msgstr "Alih-alih mengimplementasikan inverse noise channel dengan mengambil sample-nya pada QPU seperti pada probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), kita menerapkannya secara klasik pada observable yang diukur menggunakan Pauli propagation. Observable yang dihasilkan secara efektif memitigasi noise gate yang telah dipelajari saat diukur.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![PNA overview](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/pna_overview.avif)\n"
msgstr "![PNA overview](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/pna_overview.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modular error mitigation with Samplomatic and Executor {#modular-error-mitigation-with-samplomatic-and-executor}"
msgstr "Error mitigation modular dengan Samplomatic dan Executor {#modular-error-mitigation-with-samplomatic-and-executor}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The PNA approach builds upon a modular error-mitigation architecture in Qiskit. This architecture uses the [`samplomatic`](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic) library together with the `QuantumProgram` and `Executor` classes (added to Qiskit Runtime in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.47.0) to make techniques such as propagated noise absorption and Pauli twirling composable and reusable across different experiments.\n"
msgstr "Pendekatan PNA dibangun di atas arsitektur error-mitigation modular di Qiskit. Arsitektur ini menggunakan library [`samplomatic`](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic) bersama dengan kelas `QuantumProgram` dan `Executor` (ditambahkan ke Qiskit Runtime dalam `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.47.0) untuk membuat teknik seperti propagated noise absorption dan Pauli twirling menjadi composable dan reusable di berbagai eksperimen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rather than embedding the mitigation logic inside the circuit definition itself, the mitigation is expressed declaratively through `samplomatic` annotations and managed programmatically through `Executor`, which controls how randomized circuits are generated, executed, and post-processed.\n"
msgstr "Alih-alih menyematkan logika mitigation di dalam definisi circuit itu sendiri, mitigation diekspresikan secara deklaratif melalui annotation `samplomatic` dan dikelola secara programatik melalui `Executor`, yang mengontrol bagaimana circuit acak dihasilkan, dieksekusi, dan diproses lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial we implement a [Qiskit pattern](/guides/intro-to-patterns) to demonstrate how PNA can propagate inverse Pauli noise channels and modify the observable accordingly, to improve estimation of expectation values on noisy QPUs.\n"
msgstr "Dalam tutorial ini kita mengimplementasikan sebuah [Qiskit pattern](/guides/intro-to-patterns) untuk mendemonstrasikan bagaimana PNA bisa mempropagasikan inverse Pauli noise channel dan memodifikasi observable sesuai kebutuhan, untuk meningkatkan estimasi expectation value pada QPU yang noisy.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow overview {#workflow-overview}"
msgstr "Ringkasan alur kerja {#workflow-overview}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1: Map to the quantum problem**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 1: Memetakan ke masalah kuantum**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct a mirrored Trotterized kicked-Ising model and a target observable.\n"
msgstr "Membangun model kicked-Ising Trotterized yang dicerminkan dan sebuah observable target.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 2: Characterize and propagate noise**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 2: Mengkarakterisasi dan mempropagasikan noise**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `samplomatic` to identify and annotate unique two-qubit layers and measurements in the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan `samplomatic` untuk mengidentifikasi dan mengannotasi layer dua-qubit unik dan measurement dalam circuit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise affecting each unique layer using `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"
msgstr "Mempelajari noise yang memengaruhi setiap layer unik menggunakan `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map each `InjectNoise` annotation to its corresponding learned noise model.\n"
msgstr "Memetakan setiap annotation `InjectNoise` ke noise model yang dipelajari yang bersesuaian.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `qiskit-addon-pna` to propagate the inverse noise channels forward through the circuit and absorb them into the target observable.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan `qiskit-addon-pna` untuk mempropagasikan inverse noise channel maju melalui circuit dan menyerapnya ke dalam observable target.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 3: Execute quantum experiments**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 3: Mengeksekusi eksperimen kuantum**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define a `QuantumProgram` to specify randomized sampling via `samplex` and execute the experiments on the backend using the `Executor`.\n"
msgstr "Mendefinisikan sebuah `QuantumProgram` untuk menentukan randomized sampling melalui `samplex` dan mengeksekusi eksperimen pada backend menggunakan `Executor`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 4: Reconstruct and analyze results**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 4: Merekonstruksi dan menganalisis hasil**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare mitigation strategies (PNA, PNA+TREX, PNA+PS, PNA+PS+TREX) and visualize the improvement over unmitigated results.\n"
msgstr "Membandingkan strategi mitigation (PNA, PNA+TREX, PNA+PS, PNA+PS+TREX) dan memvisualisasikan peningkatan dibandingkan hasil yang tidak dimitigasi.\n"

